Article 3 For the purposes of these Regulations, foreign exchange refers to the following means of payment and assets denominated in foreign currencies that may be used for international settlement:
(1) foreign currency cash, including banknotes and coins;
(2) foreign currency payment instruments or payment tools, including bills, bank deposit certificates, bank cards, etc.;
(3) foreign currency securities, including bonds, stocks, etc.;
(4) Special Drawing Rights;
(5) other foreign exchange assets.

Article 33 When performing their duties according to law, the foreign exchange administration authorities shall have the power to take the following measures:
(1) carry out on-site inspections of financial institutions engaged in foreign exchange business;
(2) enter the places where suspected illegal foreign exchange acts are committed to investigate and collect evidence;
(3) inquire of the institutions and individuals involved in foreign exchange receipts and payments or foreign exchange business activities, and require them to provide explanations on matters directly related to the foreign exchange illegal acts under investigation;
(4) consult and copy the transaction documents and other materials directly related to the foreign exchange illegal acts under investigation;
(5) consult and copy the financial accounting materials and related documents of the parties to the foreign exchange illegal acts under investigation and the units and individuals directly involved, and may seal up the documents and materials that may be transferred, concealed or damaged;
(6) upon approval of the head of the foreign exchange administration department of the State Council or the provincial-level foreign exchange administration authority, inquire into the accounts of the parties to the foreign exchange illegal acts under investigation and the units and individuals directly involved, except for personal savings deposit accounts;
(7) where there is evidence proving that illegal funds and other related property have been or may be transferred or concealed, or that important evidence has been or may be concealed, forged or damaged, apply to a People's Court for freezing or seizure.
The relevant units and individuals shall cooperate with the supervision and inspection of the foreign exchange administration authorities, truthfully provide information on the relevant circumstances and provide relevant documents and materials, and shall not refuse, obstruct or conceal.

Article 47 Where a financial institution is in any of the following circumstances, the foreign exchange administration authorities shall order rectification within a specified time limit, confiscate the illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1 million yuan; if the circumstances are serious or the institution fails to rectify within the time limit, the foreign exchange administration authorities shall order it to cease the relevant business:
(1) failing to conduct reasonable review of the authenticity of transaction documents and their consistency with foreign exchange receipts and payments when handling fund receipts and payments under the current account;
(2) handling fund receipts and payments under the capital account in violation of the provisions;
(3) handling exchange settlement and sale business in violation of the provisions;
(4) violating the comprehensive position management of foreign exchange business;
(5) violating the administration of foreign exchange market transactions.

Article 48 Where any person is in any of the following circumstances, the foreign exchange administration authorities shall order rectification, give a warning, and may impose a fine of not more than 300,000 yuan on an institution, or not more than 50,000 yuan on an individual:
(1) failing to make statistical declaration of the balance of payments in accordance with the provisions;
(2) failing to submit financial accounting reports, statistical statements or other materials in accordance with the provisions;
(3) failing to submit valid documents as required or submitting false documents;
(4) violating the provisions on administration of foreign exchange accounts;
(5) violating the provisions on administration of foreign exchange registration;
(6) refusing or obstructing the foreign exchange administration authorities in conducting supervision, inspection or investigation according to law.
